portable-os-admin (0.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=low

  * Install as a system Python package instead of a private virtualenv, so
    the package no longer downloads anything at install time. Drop the
    Textual TUI, whose only reason to exist -- textual 0.1.13 in Debian
    bookworm -- went with it; the GUI is the only interface now.
  * Ask the desktop for administrator rights through polkit instead of
    running the application setuid or asking for a password ourselves.
  * pkexec depends on policykit-1 as an alternative: it only became its own
    package in Debian 12, and this changelog entry describes what the
    package looks like now, on a system that may be older.
  * Add cpio to Recommends: install/image_catalog.py reads a RedOS image's
    timezone and keyboard layout data through rpm2cpio | cpio directly, with
    no bsdtar fallback for that particular path.

 -- PureshkaM <xripmax@gmail.com>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

portable-os-admin (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Initial packaging: installs the admin TUI plus its Python
    dependencies (into a private virtualenv, since Debian's own
    python3-textual is far too old for this project) and pulls in
    parted, cryptsetup, debootstrap as system dependencies.

 -- PureshkaM <xripmax@gmail.com>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
